**ref › Refactor non-ref-forwarding class components**

Support for non-ref-forwarding class components in the `component` prop or as immediate `children` has been dropped.

If you were using `unstable_createStrictModeTheme` or didn't see any warnings related to `findDOMNode` in `React.StrictMode` then you don't need to take any further action.

Otherwise check out the [Caveat with refs](https://v5.mui.com/material-ui/guides/composition/#caveat-with-refs) section in the Composition guide to find out how to migrate.
This change affects almost all components where you're using the `component` prop or passing `children` to components that require `children` to be elements (for example `<MenuList><CustomMenuItem /></MenuList>`).

---

**ref › Fix ref type specificity**

For some components, you may get a type error when passing `ref`.
To avoid the error, you should use a specific element type.
For example, `Card` expects the type of `ref` to be `HTMLDivElement`, and `ListItem` expects its `ref` type to be `HTMLLIElement`.

Here is an example:

```diff
 import * as React from 'react';
 import Card from '@mui/material/Card';
 import ListItem from '@mui/material/ListItem';

 export default function SpecificRefType() {
-  const cardRef = React.useRef<HTMLElement>(null);
+  const cardRef = React.useRef<HTMLDivElement>(null);

-  const listItemRef = React.useRef<HTMLElement>(null);
+  const listItemRef = React.useRef<HTMLLIElement>(null);
   return (
     <div>
       <Card ref={cardRef}></Card>
       <ListItem ref={listItemRef}></ListItem>
     </div>
   );
 }
```

Here are the specific element types that each component expects:

#### @mui/material

- [Accordion](https://v5.mui.com/material-ui/api/accordion/) - `HTMLDivElement`
- [Alert](https://v5.mui.com/material-ui/api/alert/) - `HTMLDivElement`
- [Avatar](https://v5.mui.com/material-ui/api/avatar/) - `HTMLDivElement`
- [ButtonGroup](https://v5.mui.com/material-ui/api/button-group/) - `HTMLDivElement`
- [Card](https://v5.mui.com/material-ui/api/card/) - `HTMLDivElement`
- [Dialog](https://v5.mui.com/material-ui/api/dialog/) - `HTMLDivElement`
- [ImageList](https://v5.mui.com/material-ui/api/image-list/) - `HTMLUListElement`
- [List](https://v5.mui.com/material-ui/api/list/) - `HTMLUListElement`
- [Tab](https://v5.mui.com/material-ui/api/tab/) - `HTMLDivElement`
- [Tabs](https://v5.mui.com/material-ui/api/tabs/) - `HTMLDivElement`
- [ToggleButton](https://v5.mui.com/material-ui/api/toggle-button/) - `HTMLButtonElement`

#### @mui/lab

- [Timeline](https://v5.mui.com/material-ui/api/timeline/) - `HTMLUListElement`

